# Line endings are decided here rather than by whatever core.autocrlf each clone happens to carry.
# Nearly everything in this repository is read on Linux — by /bin/sh, by docker compose, by nginx,
# by Spotless — and a CRLF that survives the trip fails there and only there: `\r: not found` from a
# script, an invalid project name from a sourced variable, a whole file rewritten by the formatter.
# One rule for all of it, so a Windows checkout and the runner read the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except the one file Windows reads, where cmd.exe wants its own ending.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
